From f267c01361027cfc07564e250cfd25987758d958 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 02:01:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Close every HDF5 handle writers create; create nested groups
 level by level

h5_write() returned its dataset handle open and no caller closed it, and
create_group() results were discarded unclosed. Those handles keep the file
open until R's garbage collector finalises them, which is why hdf5r's
H5File$close_all() starts with a full gc(); for writers such as
write_labeled_vec() that gc() dominated the cost of writing a small file.

- h5_write() closes the dataset by default (close = FALSE keeps it open and
  returns it, as before).
- Every create_group() whose handle was discarded now closes it.
- ensure_h5_groups() no longer calls h5$exists() on the full path first:
  H5Lexists() errors when an intermediate group is missing, so writing
  '/a/b/x' into a file without '/a' failed.

After write_labeled_vec() only the file handle is open, so callers can
close it with $close() instead of $close_all().

Test: tests/testthat/test-h5-handles-closed.R (fails before this change).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AAa4DkLdNNRJxg4kNBsa7M
